H3359.strongs:
Origin: from 6965 and 3050; Jah will rise;
Meaning: Jekamjah, the name of two Israelites
KJV renders: Jekamiah. Compare 3079.

H3360.strongs:
Origin: from 6965 and 5971; (the) people will rise;
Meaning: Jekamam, an Israelite
KJV renders: Jekameam. Compare 3079, 3361.

H3361.strongs:
Origin: from 6965 and 5971; (the) people will be raised;
Meaning: Jokmeam, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Jokmeam. Compare 3360, 3362.

H3362.strongs:
Origin: from 6969 and 5971; (the) people will be lamented;
Meaning: Jokneam, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Jokneam.

H3363.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to sever oneself, i.e. (by implication) to be dislocated; figuratively, to abandon; causatively, to impale (and thus allow to drop to pieces by rotting)
KJV renders: be alienated, depart, hang (up), be out of joint.

H3364.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to awake (intransitive)
KJV renders: (be) awake(-d).

H3365.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, apparently, to be heavy, i.e. (figuratively) valuable; causatively, to make rare (figuratively, to inhibit)
KJV renders: be (make) precious, be prized, be set by, withdraw.

H3366.strongs:
Origin: from 3365;
Meaning: value, i.e. (concretely) wealth; abstractly, costliness, dignity
KJV renders: honour, precious (things), price.

H3368.strongs:
Origin: from 3365;
Meaning: valuable (objectively or subjectively)
KJV renders: brightness, clear, costly, excellent, fat, honourable women, precious, reputation.

H3369.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to ensnare (literally or figuratively)
KJV renders: fowler (lay a) snare.

H3370.strongs:
Origin: from 3369; insidious;
Meaning: Jokshan, an Arabian patriarch
KJV renders: Jokshan.

H3371.strongs:
Origin: probably from the same as 3348 and 410; veneration of God (compare 3354);
Meaning: Joktheel, the name of a place in Palestine, and of one in Idumaea
KJV renders: Joktheel.

H3372.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to fear; morally to revere; causatively to frighten
KJV renders: affright, be (make) afraid, dread(-ful), (put in) fear(-ful, -fully, -ing), (be had in) reverence(-end), × see, terrible (act, -ness, thing).

H3373.strongs:
Origin: from 3372;
Meaning: fearing; morally, reverent
KJV renders: afraid, fear (-ful).

H3374.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 3373;
Meaning: fear (also used as infinitive); morally, reverence
KJV renders: × dreadful, × exceedingly, fear(-fulness).

H3375.strongs:
Origin: from 3372; fearfulness;
Meaning: Jiron, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Iron.

H3376.strongs:
Origin: from 3373 and 3050; fearful of Jah;
Meaning: Jirijah, an Israelite
KJV renders: Irijah.

H3377.strongs:
Origin: from 7378; he will contend;
Meaning: Jareb, a symbolical name for Assyria
KJV renders: Jareb. Compare 3402.

H3378.strongs:
Origin: from 7378 and 1168; Baal will contend;
Meaning: Jerubbaal, a symbolic name of Gideon
KJV renders: Jerubbaal.

H3379.strongs:
Origin: from 7378 and 5971; (the) people will contend;
Meaning: Jarobam, the name of two Israelite kings
KJV renders: Jeroboam.

H3380.strongs:
Origin: from 7378 and 1322; shame (i.e. the idol) will contend;
Meaning: Jerubbesheth, a symbolic name for Gideon
KJV renders: Jerubbesheth.

H3381.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to descend (literally, to go downwards; or conventionally to a lower region, as the shore, a boundary, the enemy, etc.; or figuratively, to fall); causatively, to bring down (in all the above applications)
KJV renders: × abundantly, bring down, carry down, cast down, (cause to) come(-ing) down, fall (down), get down, go(-ing) down(-ward), hang down, × indeed, let down, light (down), put down (off), (cause to, let) run down, sink, subdue, take down.

H3382.strongs:
Origin: from 3381; a descent;
Meaning: Jered, the name of an antediluvian, and of an Israelite
KJV renders: Jared.

H3383.strongs:
Origin: from 3381; a descender;
Meaning: Jarden, the principal river of Palestine
KJV renders: Jordan.

H3384.strongs:
Origin: or (2 Chronicles 26:15) יָרָא; a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to flow as water (i.e. to rain); transitively, to lay or throw (especially an arrow, i.e. to shoot); figuratively, to point out (as if by aiming the finger), to teach
KJV renders: ( ) archer, cast, direct, inform, instruct, lay, shew, shoot, teach(-er,-ing), through.

H3385.strongs:
Origin: from 3384 and 410; founded of God;
Meaning: Jeruel, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Jeruel.

H3386.strongs:
Origin: perhaps denominative from 3394; (born at the) new moon;
Meaning: Jaroach, an Israelite
KJV renders: Jaroah.

H3387.strongs:
Origin: from 3417;
Meaning: green, i.e. an herb
KJV renders: green thing.

H3388.strongs:
Origin: or יְרוּשָׁה feminine passive participle of 3423; possessed;
Meaning: Jerusha or Jerushah, as Israelitess
KJV renders: Jerusha, Jerushah.

H3389.strongs:
Origin: rarely יְרוּשָׁלַיִם; a dual (in allusion to its two main hills (the true pointing, at least of the former reading, seems to be that of 3390)); probably from (the passive participle of) 3384 and 7999; founded peaceful;
Meaning: Jerushalaim or Jerushalem, the capital city of Palestine
KJV renders: Jerusalem.

H3391.strongs:
Origin: from a unused root of uncertain signification;
Meaning: a lunation, i.e. month
KJV renders: month, moon.

H3392.strongs:
Origin: the same as 3391;
Meaning: Jerach, an Arabian patriarch
KJV renders: Jerah.

H3393.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 3391;
Meaning: a month
KJV renders: month.

H3394.strongs:
Origin: from the same as 3391;
Meaning: the moon
KJV renders: moon. Yrechow. See 3405.

H3395.strongs:
Origin: from 7355; compassionate;
Meaning: Jerocham, the name of seven or eight Israelites
KJV renders: Jeroham.

H3396.strongs:
Origin: from 7355 and 410; God will compassionate;
Meaning: Jerachmeel, the name of three Israelites
KJV renders: Jerahmeel.

H3397.strongs:
Origin: patronymically from 3396;
Meaning: a Jerachmeelite or descendant of Jerachmeel
KJV renders: Jerahmeelites.

H3398.strongs:
Origin: probably of Egyptian origin;
Meaning: Jarcha, an Egyptian
KJV renders: Jarha.

H3399.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to precipitate or hurl (rush) headlong; (intransitively) to be rash
KJV renders: be perverse, turn over.
